        "id": 2007857998,
        "content": "I think this would be fairly easy to implement. Since we are using Cloudflare Pages we can use Pages functions. When a developer comes on the website from a tracker url, we store the ID in the params of the url in local storage and after they sign in with Github a JWT token is stored to local storage which we send to the function along with ID from the param. The function checks if JWT token is valid (because we have the private key of the github app) and stores ID of the signed in user and ID of the person who invited them in a DB or maybe KV so that we don't need to bother with setting up a DB.",
