        "id": 2008148491,
        "content": "Custom events: https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/collection/ga4/event-parameters?client_type=gtag#set-up-every-event\r\nHow it works:\r\n1. Referral opens `https://work.ubq.fi?utm_campaign=EthSeoul&utm_content=diamondnegroni`\r\n2. `diamondnegroni` is saved in browser's local storage\r\n3. When referral is authenticated via github then send custom event to Google Analytics:\r\n```\r\ngtag('event', 'registration', {\r\n  'referral': 'diamondnegroni',\r\n  'referrer': 'rndquu'\r\n});\r\n```\r\nI think using Google Analytics is less error prone compared to \"custom\" analytics in supabase",
        "url": "https://github.com/ubiquity/work.ubq.fi/issues/30#issuecomment-2008148491",
